Complete Project Report — my-website
A handover document summarising everything I learned about this project during our session. Written so you (or another developer, or a fresh AI chat) can pick up without re-discovering it.

1. Stack & environment
Item	Value
Framework	Laravel (v11/12 era, based on InvokeDeferredCallbacks, ValidatePathEncoding middleware)
Auth	Laravel Breeze (Blade stack)
Frontend build	Vite 7.3.6
CSS	Tailwind CSS v3 (config uses export default, @tailwind base/components/utilities)
Form plugin	@tailwindcss/forms
Server (local dev)	php artisan serve on http://127.0.0.1:8000
Project path	C:\Users\marcl\Desktop\my-website
OS	Windows
Shell	PowerShell
Editor	VS Code
2. Routes (routes/web.php)
Public:

GET / → welcome

GET /page/{slug} → PageController@show → pages.show

GET /posts → PostController@publicIndex → posts.index

GET /posts/{slug} → PostController@publicShow → posts.show

GET /category/{slug} → PostController@publicByCategory → categories.show

Admin (group: middleware('auth'), prefix('admin'), name('admin.')):

Route::resource('pages', PageController::class)

POST posts/upload-image → PostController@uploadImage → admin.posts.upload_image

Route::resource('posts', PostController::class)

Route::resource('categories', CategoryController::class)

GET|POST|PUT|DELETE /menu → MenuItemController

GET|PUT /settings → Admin\SettingController

Breeze:

GET /dashboard → redirects to admin.pages.index

/profile — inline closures for edit/update/destroy

/auth/* — loaded from routes/auth.php

3. Controllers
File	Notes
app\Http\Controllers\PageController.php	Public + admin. create() returns admin.pages.create.
app\Http\Controllers\Admin\PageController.php	Second pages controller. create() also returns admin.pages.create. Two PageControllers exist.
app\Http\Controllers\PostController.php	Posts. Has uploadImage for CKEditor.
app\Http\Controllers\CategoryController.php	Categories.
app\Http\Controllers\MenuItemController.php	Menu builder.
app\Http\Controllers\Admin\SettingController.php	Settings.
4. Models
Page — title, slug, content, is_published, is_admin_only

Post — title, category_id, content, is_published, likely excerpt

Category — name, slug

MenuItem — menu builder entries

Setting — key/value table (key, value). Accessed via \App\Models\Setting::pluck('value', 'key')

5. Layouts
Two parallel layouts. This is the biggest source of confusion in the project.

layouts/admin.blade.php — custom admin layout
Used via @extends('layouts.admin') + @section('content')

Has @php block that loads $globalSettings (or queries Setting::pluck) and defines $primaryColor, $accentColor, $textColor, $headingFont, $bodyFont, $borderRadius, $containerWidth, $headerBgColor, $headerImage

Outputs CSS variables in <style>: --primary-color, --accent-color, --text-color, --heading-font, --body-font, --border-radius

Loads @vite(['resources/css/app.css', 'resources/js/app.js'])

Includes @include('layouts.navigation')

Renders @yield('content')

Has CKEditor content styling rules for .ck-content classes

Has body { color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); } and h1..h6 { font-family: var(--heading-font); } rules (added during this session)

layouts/app.blade.php — Breeze layout
Used via <x-app-layout> component (App\View\Components\AppLayout → render() returns view('layouts.app'))

Has the same @php settings block and CSS variables

Uses {{ $slot }} (changed from @yield('content') during this session, because <x-app-layout> passes content as a slot, not a section)

Has @isset($header) block for named slot rendering

Still loads CKEditor CDN <link> and <script> tags in <head> — leftover from earlier, harmless but unnecessary

layouts/navigation.blade.php
Shared nav, includes site name, nav links, admin links, user dropdown

layouts/guest.blade.php
Auth pages

